{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.proton_mass_substrate_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.proton_mass_substrate_identity","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L66-L76","doc":"**Proton-mass substrate identity (conditional on `ProtonBorromeanAssembly`).**\n\nGiven the conjectural Borromean assembly, the proton mass equals the published\nflat form `2·m_μ·F_Bor − 12·m_e`; the concrete integers are DERIVED\n(`2 = multiplicity`, `12 = multiplicity · bindingCount = 2 · 6`), not assumed.\nSorry-free modulo the single class instance. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.assembly","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Conjectural assembly law — the proton mass is the multiplicity times the\nper-constituent (muon-dressed minus electron-bound) mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.bindingCount_eq_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.bindingCount_eq_six","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.bindingCount","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.bindingCount","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Conjectural input 2 — the per-constituent electron-binding count is\n`|S₃| = 6` (the Ocneanu −1/12 leading-pole inverse). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.multiplicity_eq_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.multiplicity_eq_two","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L57-L57","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.multiplicity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.multiplicity","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Conjectural input 1 — the constituent multiplicity is `dim V_(2,1) = 2`\n(the trace-dominant Hecke irrep dimension). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.protonMass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.protonMass","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L53-L53","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.fBor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.fBor","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L52-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.mE","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.mE","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L51-L51","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.mMu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.mMu","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L50-L50","doc":"muon mass (CAL-2 derived), electron mass (CAL-1), Borromean observable\nvalue `F_Bor(q₀)`, and the proton mass. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly.mk","kind":"ctor","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixQValues.ProtonBorromeanAssembly","kind":"class","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixQValues/ProtonBorromeanAssembly.lean#L39-L64","doc":"**Conjecture: the proton's Borromean mass assembly**\n(`conj:proton-borromean-assembly`).\n\nThe fields are the conjectural categorical *hypotheses* (the two\nstructural-integer identifications and the assembly law in factored form); the\nsubstrate identity is *derived* from them (`proton_mass_substrate_identity`),\nso this is a genuine §3b-cond conditional input, not a self-assuming\nprojection of the conclusion. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:proton-borromean-assembly","label":"conj:proton-borromean-assembly","md":"quantum-observable-universe/appendix-qvalues/proton-borromean-assembly.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}